<BaseLayout title="Real Estate Due Diligence & Valuation | Lake Como Property Advisory" active="services" description="Property due diligence and valuation support around Lake Como, including condition, planning constraints, risks and IVS-informed valuation.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb">Home / <a href="/services/">Services</a> / Due diligence & valuation</div><span class="eyebrow">04 · Due diligence & valuation</span><h1 style="margin-top:20px">Look beyond<br />the first impression.</h1><p class="lead">Understand a property’s potential, constraints and risks before you commit.</p></div></section>
  <div class="page-hero-image"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600607687939-ce8a6c25118c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2000&q=88" alt="Contemporary residence and landscaped garden" /></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container detail-grid"><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="eyebrow">Know what you are buying</span><h3 style="margin-top:16px">A structured view of the property and its context.</h3><p>Independent analysis can help frame questions, identify red flags and prioritise further investigations.</p><a class="btn" href="/#contact">Request an initial discussion <span>↗</span></a></aside><div class="detail-copy"><p class="lead">A beautiful setting is only one part of a sound property decision. Due diligence brings together the information needed to assess suitability, risk and potential next steps.</p><h2>Property due diligence</h2><ul><li>Review of available property documents and known planning information.</li><li>Coordination of technical inspections by suitable specialists.</li><li>Identification of visible condition concerns and items requiring further investigation.</li><li>Review of renovation potential, likely work packages and preliminary cost considerations.</li><li>Coordination with legal, tax, cadastral and planning professionals where required.</li></ul><h2>Valuation informed by recognised standards</h2><p>Where valuation services are commissioned, the scope and method should be appropriate to the purpose, property and available evidence. International Valuation Standards (IVS) can provide a recognised framework for consistent valuation practice. Formal valuation reports requiring specific professional status or statutory authority will be referred to appropriately qualified valuers.</p><p>Our role can include market and property research, information gathering, preliminary value considerations and coordination of a formal independent valuation where appropriate. Any conclusion must be clearly identified according to its scope and limitations.</p><h2>Clear findings. Better questions.</h2><p>The output is designed to help you understand what is known, what remains uncertain and which checks should happen before a decision is made.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Important</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">A preliminary review is not a substitute for legal title checks, structural surveys, environmental investigations or a formal valuation report where these are required.</p></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
